<title>USA: Interra nominates Mondale to its board.</title>
<headline>Interra nominates Mondale to its board.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interra Financial Inc said Wednesday it nominated former U.S. vice president Walter Mondale to its board, to stand for election at the company's April 30 annual meeting.</p>
<p>If elected, Mondale would increase the size of the company's board to 10 members from nine. He would become the seventh non-management director.</p>
<p>Interra, formerly Inter-Regional Financial Group Inc, is the parent company of regional brokerage-dealers Dain Bosworth in Minneapolis and Rauscher Pierce Refsnes in Dallas, Texas.</p>
<p>	    ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
